From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] write the inverse of the white balance gains as AsShotNeutral

libdng_set_neutral() and makedng --neutral take white balance gains, as
the API docs and the man page say, and Megapixels passes its gains. But
they were written to AsShotNeutral as they are, and AsShotNeutral is the
raw value of a neutral colour: the inverse of the gains. A DNG converter
then applied the white balance the wrong way round, and photos came out
with the opposite colour cast, doubled.

Write gain[green] / gain[i], and convert back the same way when reading,
so the API keeps meaning gains in both directions. Reading also no longer
copies more than three values into neutral[3].

---
--- a/docs/api.rst	2025-11-11 03:01:35.000000000 +0400
+++ n/docs/api.rst	2026-10-12 23:47:16.635394516 +0400
@@ -300,6 +300,9 @@
 
    libdng_free(&dng);
 
+The DNG stores the inverse of these gains, the raw value of a neutral colour,
+in AsShotNeutral; libdng converts both ways.
+
 Affected tags:
 
 - TIFFTAG_ASSHOTNEUTRAL
--- a/src/libdng.c	2025-11-11 03:01:35.000000000 +0400
+++ n/src/libdng.c	2026-10-12 23:47:16.635059865 +0400
@@ -456,7 +456,16 @@
 		TIFFSetField(tif, DNGTAG_FORWARD_MATRIX_1, 9, dng->forward_matrix_1);
 	if(!is_empty_matrix(dng->forward_matrix_2))
 		TIFFSetField(tif, DNGTAG_FORWARD_MATRIX_2, 9, dng->forward_matrix_2);
-	TIFFSetField(tif, DNGTAG_ASSHOTNEUTRAL, 3, dng->neutral);
+	/*
+	 * dng->neutral holds white balance gains, as libdng_set_neutral()
+	 * documents. AsShotNeutral is the raw value of a neutral colour, which
+	 * is the inverse of those gains.
+	 */
+	float as_shot_neutral[3];
+	for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
+		as_shot_neutral[i] = dng->neutral[i] > 0.0f ? dng->neutral[1] / dng->neutral[i] : 1.0f;
+	}
+	TIFFSetField(tif, DNGTAG_ASSHOTNEUTRAL, 3, as_shot_neutral);
 	TIFFSetField(tif, DNGTAG_ANALOGBALANCE, 3, dng->analogbalance);
 
 	if (dng->camera_make != NULL)
@@ -627,9 +636,10 @@
 	}
 	TIFFGetField(tif, TIFFTAG_ORIENTATION, &dng->orientation);
 
-	if (TIFFGetField(tif, DNGTAG_ASSHOTNEUTRAL, &count, &fvalues) == 1) {
-		for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
-			dng->neutral[i] = fvalues[i];
+	if (TIFFGetField(tif, DNGTAG_ASSHOTNEUTRAL, &count, &fvalues) == 1 && count == 3) {
+		/* Back from the raw value of neutral to gains */
+		for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
+			dng->neutral[i] = fvalues[i] > 0.0f ? fvalues[1] / fvalues[i] : 1.0f;
 		}
 	}
 	if (TIFFGetField(tif, DNGTAG_ANALOGBALANCE, &count, &fvalues) == 1) {
